<Article title="Dead Hang Equipment Reviews: Evidence & Buying Criteria" description="How DeadHangs evaluates equipment information: mounting requirements, fit, documented specifications and clear affiliate disclosures.">
<div class="article-header"><div class="article-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>How we assess dead hang equipment.</div><h1 class="article-h1">How we assess dead hang equipment.</h1><p class="article-subtitle">Our buying guides compare equipment information. We do not claim hands-on testing unless a review includes a documented test.</p></div>
<div class="article-body"><h2>What a useful review needs</h2><p>A useful equipment review explains who the product fits and what must be checked before buying. Mounting requirements, available space and the manufacturer's instructions come before a recommendation.</p><ul><li>Identify the exact model and the current manufacturer documentation.</li><li>State the mounting surface, doorway measurements or floor space required.</li><li>Separate manufacturer specifications from observations made during a documented test.</li><li>Describe limitations and the likely reason to choose another category.</li><li>Link the reader to current availability rather than presenting an undated price as current.</li></ul><h2>Our testing disclosure</h2><p>Earlier wording on this page described a multi-week testing programme and verified load tests. We do not have the records needed to substantiate those claims. That wording has been removed. The current equipment guide is a research-based buying guide.</p><p>A future hands-on review must identify the model, test date, setup and actual observations. It must also explain any limitations. We will not award a verified load rating from an informal home test.</p><h2>Choose the mounting category first</h2><p>A doorway bar, fixed wall bar and free-standing station solve different space problems. Installation requirements vary between products in the same category. Read the exact manufacturer's instructions before buying or fitting one.</p><p>Start with the <a href="/equipment-guide/">dead hang equipment guide</a> for the category comparison and buying checks.</p><h2>How affiliate links affect the site</h2><p>Some retailer links earn a commission if you purchase. The guide labels these links and identifies the retailer region. An affiliate relationship does not prove a product has been tested here.</p><p>See our <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> for source and disclosure rules.</p><h2>Report a specification change</h2><p>Include the product name and the manufacturer's current documentation when reporting a correction. We can then compare the claim with the source.</p><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> to send feedback.</p></div>
</Article>
